==Strategy==
Given the difficulty of this stage, having either [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] or UL Legends such as [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] is highly recommended.

This is a chaotic Behemoth stage with the dual menace of Rangmaster and Hazuku supported by annoying peons and Zapy being the main thing to focus on here. Fighting Rangmaster and Hazuku and overbuffed peons is not enjoyable whatsoever, meaning that your priority is rushing down the Rangmaster before Hazuku can do too much. As such, make sure to kill the Celeboodle with [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and to use a Rich Cat if you don't have access to powerful Ubers or UL Legends. With either a powerful Anti-Aku meatshield like [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]] or simply cycling two fast meatshields like [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and a first/second form [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]], Rangmaster should be stalled pretty well until any peons come in. To ensure you're able to kill Rangmaster fast, bring a Shield Piercer like [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] and a strong backliner to demolish Rangmaster like [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]], Awakened Naala, Esoteric Uril, or if you're truly desperate, [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]]. [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] in general should be able to take care of the peons, meaning that it shouldn't be too hard to demolish Rangmaster even with occasional annoying peon support. With him down, your next priority is killing Hazuku, which will not be easy given the Zapy and peons. As such, after killing Rangmaster try to get a small stack of units such that they will get into Hazuku's blindspot but not hit the base too much, as doing so spawns a nasty Puffington that complicates matters a lot. From here, your goal is hoping Hazuku doesn't randomly Surge all your units while you work on killing Zapy. [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] is extremely strong here, being able to live a Hazuku hit even on 120% and having high enough damage to quickly whittle down the Zapy. Try to aim for Chief or one of your other Z-Killers to kill Zapy, although if you can't get a Z-Kill on Zapy, it's not the end of the world, as you can now spam as many of your damage dealers as you want like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] without having to worry about Zapy not getting Z-Killed. Once Hazuku goes down, you've effectively won, although be careful of the Puffington and Sir Rels on base hit.

===Recommended Ubers===
*Anti-Aku nukers are great here to demolish Rangmaster fast. Examples include [[White Knight Cyclops (Uber Rare Cat)|Demon Knight Kyklops]], [[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Obliterator Diabolosa]], [[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Amaterasu]] and [[Amakusa Shiro (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Amakusa]].
*If you are fortunate enough to own [[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Netherworld Nymph Lunacia]], she can be used to defeat Rangmaster quickly with her shield pierce and guaranteed weaken to then heavily damage or outright destroy the base in a single rush.

